    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c0a7db8f_bd6df2ab",
        "filename": "zephyr/subsys/pd_controller/pdc_dpm.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 264,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-10T17:18:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If 3A_PORTS \u003d\u003d 0, then we won\u0027t enable FRS until after evaluating the source caps, even if the FRS partner only wants 1.5A.\n\nThis is the safer thing to do, but it could lead to the same PD compliance failure on a board that doesn\u0027t support sourcing 3A.\n\nThis quirk warrants a comment.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 264,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 264,
        "endChar": 45
      },
      "revId": "840af1d01e22fdb636981bff2ff76405552db799",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b1087a2d_6975b596",
        "filename": "zephyr/subsys/pd_controller/pdc_dpm.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 264,
      "author": {
        "id": 1527433
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-17T23:05:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Added comment that it can take longer to enable FRS on platforms which can\u0027t source 3A.",
      "parentUuid": "c0a7db8f_bd6df2ab",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 264,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 264,
        "endChar": 45
      },
      "revId": "840af1d01e22fdb636981bff2ff76405552db799",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "872a1787_a35ae35c",
        "filename": "zephyr/subsys/pd_controller/pdc_power_mgmt.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 2395,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-10T17:18:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This path needs to send CMD_PDC_SET_FRS, otherwise you won\u0027t enable/disable FRS until the SNK policies are run, which occurs very late.\n\nI\u0027m not sure if the PDC retains the FRS enable/disable through disconnects.\n\nOn a disconnect, we set the Source PDO limit to 7.5W.  We don\u0027t increase the Source PDO setting until we run SNK policies (SNK_POLICY_UPDATE_SRC_CAPS).  What happens if FRS is enabled and the partner wants 15W, but the source PDO is only 7.5W?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2395,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 2395,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "840af1d01e22fdb636981bff2ff76405552db799",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "92387f8a_93dc512a",
        "filename": "zephyr/subsys/pd_controller/pdc_power_mgmt.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 2395,
      "author": {
        "id": 1527433
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-10T23:48:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for pointing this out. I\u0027ll follow up with changes to account for FRS and Src Cap being set by SNK policies.\n\n* I\u0027m not sure if the PDC retains the FRS enable/disable through disconnects.\n\nI think this could depend on the PDC. For TI, FRS is enabled/disabled by updating the Port Control Register (0x29) which I expect persists across disconnections. This change calls `pdc_power_mgmt_frs_enable` in `pdc_dpm_remove_source` to disable FRS, but as you\u0027ve pointed out that wouldn\u0027t run until SNK policies are updated. \n\n* What happens if FRS is enabled and the partner wants 15W, but the source PDO is only 7.5W?\n\nMight depend on the PDC. For TI, it will not FR swap. The PDC also checks the partner\u0027s Snk Caps against our Src Caps. From the FR Swap Enable bit of TPS6699x datasheet:\n\n*\"Assert this bit to enable Fast-Role Swap detection. If the amount of current the Port Partner requires during the Fast-Role Swap process is less than or equal to the current in Transmit Source Capabilities (TXSourcePDO1) when an FRS signal is detected, then the device will perform a Fast-Role swap\"*",
      "parentUuid": "872a1787_a35ae35c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2395,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 2395,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "840af1d01e22fdb636981bff2ff76405552db799",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a7e48742_38eef0b8",
        "filename": "zephyr/subsys/pd_controller/pdc_power_mgmt.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 2395,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-11T17:39:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We should check with RTK.  If they have a similar check, we might be able to unconditionally enable FRS and use our Src Caps to ensure we don\u0027t oversubscribe our sourcing power.",
      "parentUuid": "92387f8a_93dc512a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2395,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 2395,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "840af1d01e22fdb636981bff2ff76405552db799",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0faaa4c0_3e1074de",
        "filename": "zephyr/subsys/pd_controller/pdc_power_mgmt.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 2395,
      "author": {
        "id": 1527433
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-17T23:05:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027ve update this CL to send SET_FRS a few states after requesting 3A. This is in the same place as the current `SNK_ATTACHED_DISABLE_FRS` state.\n\nThe PDC power manager will only add the PD Src to the DPM if FRS is enabled, but will send `CMD_PDC_SET_FRS` regardless. If the DPM hasn\u0027t updated FRS, the PDC power manager defaults to false.\n\n\n\n* What happens if FRS is enabled and the partner wants 15W, but the source PDO is only 7.5W?\n\nBack to this question, it depends on the PDC. RTK says that the PDC will FR Swap anyway (b/431851876). TI\u0027s datasheet states that the PDC will not FRS, but that isn\u0027t the behavior I am seeing. I tried adding a state SNK_ATTACHED_SET_FRS to update SRC Caps, and that broke the compliance test.\n\nWith this version of the update, just updating FRS without sending a Src Cap update until SNK policies, the FRS compliance tests consistently pass.",
      "parentUuid": "a7e48742_38eef0b8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2395,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 2395,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "840af1d01e22fdb636981bff2ff76405552db799",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    }
  ]
